And what's even more unusual is that for the line DT2[ , v],  the function
`[.data.table` is never called.  I included
debug(data.table:::`[.data.table`) and nothing happened for DT2[ , v], but
it was activated for DT2[ , 2] and the other evaluations of extract on DT2.
 My hunch is that the since the S4 method is dispatching the method with a
signature that includes the classes for i and j, something is going wrong
there since it is only getting awry when the class of j is a name.  I'm
going to test out that hunch.

